implementationPlan.description:
Re-anchor scripts/tests/usage-launcher.test.mjs (the Claude and Codex arms, 6 cases per engine).

(1) Add the same guard helper next to `run`, cut from the text run() already reads (`const text = source(ext)`):
```
const guard = (ext, text) => ext === 'ps1'
  ? `$script:AgentGitGuard=$null
${between(text, 'function Invoke-MoeGuardedCommand {', 'function Remove-MoeAgentGitGuard')}
`
  : `AGENT_GIT_GUARD_ENV=()
${between(text, 'agent_git_exec() (', '
)
')}
)
`;
```
In run(), write `setup + guard(ext, text) + block + '
' + body`, so every cut launch line finds the launcher's own guard. Today the sh Codex arms exit 127 (agent_git_exec not found) and ps1 says 'Invoke-MoeGuardedCommand is not recognized'.

(2) Claude arms' end anchors moved, because 447281cf inserted guard cleanup after the launch:
- ps1 `'
        }
    }

    # Launch-failure classification'` becomes `'
        }
    }

    Remove-MoeAgentGitGuard'`;
- sh `'
    fi

    stop_heartbeat_sidecar'` becomes `'
    fi

    if [ -n "${AGENT_GIT_GUARD_ROOT:-}" ]'`.
Start anchors, the Codex cuts (`Start-MoeUsageReceipt 'codex' 'headless'` to `} else {`; `start_moe_usage_receipt codex headless` to `set -e`), the hint blocks, every fake source and every assertion stay unchanged.

No harness may strip the guard call or define its own guard. Leave scripts/moe-agent.{sh,ps1} untouched. A shared scripts/tests helper is allowed by the rail but not needed: keep each file self-contained like today.

Check with `env -u MOE_WORKER_ID node --test scripts/tests/usage-launcher.test.mjs`: it was 6 fail on /bin/bash at HEAD, now 0 fail.

Adversarial self-review (final step). Load adversarial-self-review.

(1) Scratch-only mutants on the snapshot copies. Each one must FAIL by assertion on /bin/bash, then be restored and cmp'd:
- restore the old sh exec anchor (no `agent_git_exec`): 'missing boundaries';
- drop `${guard('sh')}` from the prompt-cache script: CHILD_EXIT is not 23 (exit 127);
- drop guard(ext, text) from usage run(): the Codex arms fail;
- restore the old sh Claude end anchor: 'missing implementation boundary'.
A mutant that only fails at load (a syntax error) is not a kill.

(2) Check DoD3 and DoD4 by reading the diff:
- every cut still contains the guard call exactly as the launcher has it;
- the guard text comes only from between() over the launcher source;
- `git diff --stat -- scripts/moe-agent.sh scripts/moe-agent.ps1` shows nothing from this task;
- no assertion was removed or loosened (diff the assert lines);
- no MOE_*-dependent behavior: the gate runs under env -i.

(3) Note in complete_task that CI's ci.yml 'Test agent runtime discovery' step runs these two files on all three OSes. If a finding changes a file, rerun step 3 fresh.

